    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1855" root="بخ" body-key="b">
    
      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَخْبَخَ</span></b> , (S, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَخْبَخَةٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِخْبَاخٌ</span>, (TA,) [a verb imitative of the sound

which it signifies,] <i>He</i> (a camel [in a state of
excitement]) <i>brayed,</i> (S, K,) <i>so that his</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شِقْشِقَة</span>
[or <i>faucial bag</i>] <i>filled his mouth:</i> (S:) or, as
some say, <i>began to bray.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,
perhaps,] <i>He</i> (a man) <i>said</i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَخْ</span>] or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَخْ بَخْ</span> [&amp;c.].
(TA, and Har p. 556.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And [hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَخْبَخَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِصُحْبَتِى</span> <i>He rejoiced in my company.</i> (Har ubi
suprà.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَخْبَخَ الرَّجُلَ</span> <i>He said</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَخْ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَخْ بَخْ</span>
&amp;c. <i>to the man.</i> (S.)

